Now I'll write the play program. The AC'97 PCM Out DMA uses a Buffer Descriptor List (BDL): 32 entries of 8 bytes each — dword0 = buffer physical address, dword1 = control(bit) + length in samples (16-bit words). PCM Out box is at NABM+0x10:
- +0x10 (BDBAR): BDL base address (32-bit)
- +0x15 (LVI): last valid index
- +0x16 (SR): status
- +0x1B (CR): control — bit0 = Run/Busy (RPBM), bit1 = reset

Layout of DMA buffer: PCM at r7. I'll build the BDL in my scratch region r12 (survives). One BDL entry pointing at r7, length = r10*channels samples = r10*2 (16-bit words). Length field is in samples (16-bit units), max 0xFFFE.

